          4 OK         Error-only instrumentation on the two session-context procedures                                                                                                                                         0 of 2 have the wrong shape. Error-only means the CATCH calls logs.uspRecordExecutionError and the procedure opens NO start row: one row per request would be roughly 4.3 million a day at fifty requests a second. G-22. LastSeenUtc is the per-request record instead.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                
          4 OK         Full instrumentation on the two maintenance procedures                                                                                                                                                   0 of 2 have the wrong shape. These two are called by a person a few times a month, so every call earns a start row, a completion UPDATE and a transaction -- and a maintenance bypass nobody can account for afterwards is the failure this whole file exists to prevent.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
          4 OK         auth.uspSetSessionContext refuses a hash that is not 32 bytes (E-50100)                                                                                                                                  Error 50100. A short binary is silently right-padded by an implicit conversion, so the length is checked rather than assumed: without this, 0x00 would be compared against every stored hash, match none of them, and the caller would be told there was no such session.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               
          4 OK         auth.uspSetSessionContext refuses an unknown session (E-50020)                                                                                                                                           Error 50020. This is the whole procedure running end to end -- the session SELECT, the refusal, the CATCH and an orphan logs.ExecutionLog row with no start row before it -- without setting a single key. Appendix B: 50020 and 50023 are separate numbers because the UI does different things with them, which is why this procedure reads auth.UserSession itself instead of calling auth.udfResolveSessionUser.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
          4 OK         auth.uspClearSessionContext runs and reports no identity on this connection                                                                                                                              @IdentityKeysRemain = 0, error 0. 0 is the expected answer for a deployment connection, which is nobody. Clearing when nothing is set is a no-op by design: the pooled-connection case cannot know what the last request left behind.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   
